+// bw-port: Run speed 2x and 4x: the player's faster run step sets its animation (the run's MAP_OBJ_UNK_A0_09) and back to 0 at its
+// end; the sprite code that reads it here takes that 0 as the pause between two steps, after which the run animation goes back
+// to a multiple of 4 of its frames, so the 2-frame step (2x) drew the run's first pose for good and the 1-frame step (4x, set and
+// reset in one map-object update) drew the player standing. Through the step's frames it reads the step's animation
+// (port/game/speed_gen4.c PortSpeed4_RunStepAnim; the stored value at every other frame and setting).
